4. HLD 

if time permits here we can talk about Database basically what table of each core entity would look like


Client --> API Gateway ---> Event Crud Service ---> Cache --> Database
                       ---> Search Endpoint
                       ---> Reserve/Payment Endpoint

Now for tickets which were reseved and not bought we need to bring them back in available state we can use a cron job for that (however that creates a delta)
say job runs every 10 time now if someone books ticket at 12.01 even thou it expires at 12.11 it would become avialble only at 12.20 (9 min waste)

A better solution is to have a ticket lock using something like redis and whenver we return ticket map check if ticket is locked and than return same
immeditaley when time expires this lock is given up 


We prefer SQL DB since we need high consistency and we have compelx relationships here also (so we can go into MYSQL or PostgreSQL)


